  "notes": "The 3.09 km Cádiz Bay crossing has two forked concrete towers, four stay fans per tower, the removable deck in place, a shallow steel box girder and both approach viaducts. Aerial control and the retained PMTiles footprint determine the alignment. Global elevation controls the abutment contacts and visible foundations. The intermediate vertical alignment and pier spacing are exterior visualization estimates. The removable span is modeled in its installed position. The catalog mesh does not simulate span removal, traffic rules, structural behavior, or vessel navigation. The Puerto Real service roads remain in the native scene. The standard elevation grid does not describe their underpass clearance or detailed abutment grading. Physical-device timings are unmeasured.",
